														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3830751">
									

<p>I think it's important to note that 2718 only implies that O5-11's fate is the fate of everyone, but never proves it, and there's significant reason to doubt that. Most notably, if you highlight the space just below the log you'll get this: Ρωγερ, έχετε καταβληθεί τιμή, σοι μετατίθημι στον παράδεισο. According to its <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/SCPDeclassified/comments/6mnff4/scp2718_what_happens_after/?st=ji8bo4g5&amp;sh=38ae02c6">SCP declassified page</a>, that translates to 'Roger, your price is paid. I transport you to paradise'. So that line alone means that even if Roger Sheldon's fate is universal, it's not eternal. It's a kind of purgatory.</p>
<p>Plus, if you combine that with info from the rest of the wiki, it doesn't seem like O5-11's fate is universal or even all that common. It's my personal head canon that Roger's body was turned into a soul trap, either because of the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-dark-web-dke79-o2rg5-4jlw6">quantum retrocausal method of resurrection</a>, or maybe someone just cursed him because he was <a href="/scp-3440">an asshole who deserved it</a>.</p>

