			<div class="content" id="post-content-3830724">
									

<p>There should probably be a link to 2718 near the beginning, since it's pretty important to the story.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This has been a good series, and this is a pretty good conclusion.</p>
<p>It's not the most <em>surprising</em> conclusion &#8212; some people who've read 2718 probably could have predicted the broad strokes of this from the instant someone said &quot;Dammerung&quot; &#8212; but it's still interesting seeing how it played out.</p>
<p>Young's character receives more development here than elsewhere, appropriately making earlier articles deeper in retrospect. You get to understand a bit better why she acted the way she did in 3984, which is good.</p>
<p>I do wish there was more of a conclusion for Joyce and Eric, maybe even the D-class from 3984. Their plotlines get left a bit hanging, since we don't know how they process the news or what they do with the information. As well, we know the Foundation's general strategy moving forward, but it'd be nice to see that crystallize in a more definite form than just being a planned strategy. Those things might make for a more complete and satisfying conclusion. If that's not planned for now, I'd love to see the plotline be returned to after the contest is over.</p>
<p>Overall, this has been a great story. The sheer volume of work is incredibly impressive, and each page does a good job of filling out and exploring the world and its implications in a creative way.</p>
<p>Great job, all of you.</p>
</div>
</div>
